# ML experiments

## Logging

- Inside `mlflow.start_run()`, log params, validation metrics (log loss, Brier, accuracy, AUC), and the git SHA (`git_commit` tag).
- Experiment names in this file are the sqlite names. `activate_tracking_experiment` is the only rewrite. When the tracking URI is `databricks` or `databricks://...`, a relative name is stored under `ENDZONE_MLFLOW_EXPERIMENT_ROOT` (default `/Shared/endzone-mlops`). `nfl_pregame/registry` becomes `/Shared/endzone-mlops/nfl_pregame/registry`. A name that already starts with `/` is unchanged. sqlite and Pages keep the relative names. The parent workspace folder is created with `workspace.mkdirs` when it is missing. That call does nothing when the folder already exists.
- Model selection uses validation only. Do not read test (2025) metrics to pick a model.
- Log sklearn models with the reviewed skops trusted-types allowlist only (`REVIEWED_SKOPS_TRUSTED_TYPES`). An unknown type fails closed.
- A `--cv` invocation logs one parent run and one nested child per scored model. The parent holds `comparison.md`, `comparison.csv`, `best_feature_set`, and `data_digest`. Each child logs `decision` (`accepted`, `rejected`, `reference`, `baseline`, `benchmark`, or `inconclusive`) and `log_loss_diff`, `log_loss_diff_ci_low`, `log_loss_diff_ci_high`. `benchmark` is the H6, pkg_core, pkg_core_inj, ensembles, ensembles_r2, qbelo538, and prior_shrink market row. Other hypotheses still tag the market `baseline`. The same `data_digest` on the parent and the children means they used the same matrix. In the MLflow UI, filter with `tags.decision` and compare the child runs.

## Status

Phase 0 and Phase 1 are done. Phase 2 decisions through H5b are recorded. Phases 3 and 4 are planned and not started. Do not invent their scope. H4 is rejected. H5 is rejected, with a positive signal. H5b is rejected. The 0.003 threshold is not changed after either result. The reference stays logistic `h2_full` except where a later note names another reference. Recency and streak challengers are preregistered and not run. See `docs/experiments/recency_streak.md`. H6 is preregistered and not run. See `docs/experiments/h6_opponent_adjusted.md`. `pkg_core` is preregistered and not run. See `docs/experiments/pkg_core.md`. `pkg_core_inj` is preregistered and not run. See `docs/experiments/pkg_core_inj.md`. Ensembles are preregistered and not run. The reference for that note is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. See `docs/experiments/ensembles.md`. Ensembles round 2 is preregistered and not run. The reference for that note is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. See `docs/experiments/ensembles_r2.md`. The QB Elo comparison is preregistered and not run. The reference for that note is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. See `docs/experiments/qbelo538.md`. The prior-shrink comparison is preregistered and not run. The reference for that note is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. See `docs/experiments/prior_shrink.md`.

Sprint 2 is margin and total, not a new win-probability phase. The rule is ADR-007 and `configs/experiments/s2.yaml`, locked before the fit. Ridge on `h2_full` is accepted only when pooled CV MAE beats its baseline, the 95% paired bootstrap interval of (model MAE minus baseline MAE) lies entirely below 0, and the model is strictly better in at least 5 of 8 seasons (2016-2023). Margin baseline: Elo difference including home field, divided by 25. Total baseline: training-fold mean total. Market MAE, RMSE, 80% coverage, and implied win log loss versus 0.638 are reported and are not gates. Do not move those thresholds after a result. The warehouse CV is already in `docs/experiments/reports/sprint2_cv_report.json`. Both targets accepted, n=2191, seasons 2016-2023. Margin MAE 10.155811 versus Elo/25 10.412221 (difference -0.256409, 8 of 8 seasons). Total MAE 10.925618 versus the league mean 11.130543 (difference -0.204925, 5 of 8 seasons). Do not hand-edit that file.

