H3, CV 2016-2023, n=2191: logistic `h2_full` 0.6377. `h3_split` 0.6393 (difference +0.0016, interval -0.0009 to 0.0039). `h3_replace` 0.6395 (difference +0.0018, interval -0.0008 to 0.0043).

Ridge, same window: `logistic_l2` on `h2_full` is 0.6386 (difference +0.0009, interval -0.0008 to 0.0025) versus plain logistic `h2_full` 0.6377. `logistic_l2` `h3_split` is +0.0010. `logistic_l2` `h3_replace` is +0.0015. Fold-tuned L2 does not help. Those fits still reject the H3 splits, so the H3 rejection is not collinearity noise.

H4, same window, n=2191: logistic `h2_full` 0.6377. `h4_clean` 0.6398 (difference +0.0021, interval -0.0012 to 0.0053). `h4_clean_sr` 0.6379 (difference +0.0002, interval -0.0036 to 0.0039). Removing `no_play`, kneels, spikes, and garbage time adds no signal. Averaging over many plays already absorbs that noise. A first local run before the dbt rebuild printed the same log loss 0.6509 for both clean sets because the clean columns were absent. That number is not the comparison.

H5, same window, n=2191: logistic `h2_full` 0.6377. `h5_qb` 0.6355 (difference -0.0022, interval -0.0042 to -0.0003, AUC 0.6869). Rejected. The rule needs a gain of at least 0.003. The interval excludes zero, so the sign is a positive signal. The threshold is not changed after the result. QB-change subset, 383 out-of-fold games: difference -0.0026, interval -0.0075 to 0.0023. Depth-chart starter sides 10,249. Previous-passer fallback sides 4,399. Games flagged as a QB change: 972. H5b is the same `h5_qb` features after the starter join is fixed. H5b, same window: `h5_qb` 0.6356 (difference -0.0021, interval -0.0039 to -0.0002). Rejected. Short of -0.003. The threshold is not moved.

EPA filter (`docs/experiments/reports/epa_filter_check.md`): `play = 1` rows are pass 528,368 (53.6%), run 388,724 (39.5%), and no_play 68,233 (6.9%). No special-teams play types. Only 36 kneels and 70 spikes have `play = 1`. The contamination is the `no_play` (penalty) rows, not special teams. That finding drives H4.

Accept a Phase 2 feature set only when pooled log loss improves by at least 0.003 and the 95% interval lies entirely below 0. The ridge setup rule is separate: switch the reference to `logistic_l2` on `h2_full` only when its `log_loss_diff` is <= 0. This run did not.

## Commands

The canonical module is `python -m endzone.modeling.train`. `python -m endzone.train.train` calls the same `main` with the same flags. Hypothesis rows live in `configs/experiments/*.yaml`. Every `--cv` command uses rolling-origin seasons 2016-2023. Train on `season < S` and score `season == S`. 2024 is the final validation and is not a fold. 2025 is not scored. Each command also scores the home prior, Elo, and the market.

- Phase 1: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv`. Reference `baseline-home`. Local report `reports/phase1/`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase1_baselines`, tag `phase=1`.
- H1: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h1`. Scores logistic `current`, `diff`, and `diff_only` against logistic `current`. Local report `reports/phase2/`. Tags `phase=2`, `hypothesis=h1-diff`.
- H2: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h2 --reference-model logistic --reference-feature-set current`. Scores `current`, `h2_def`, and `h2_full` against logistic `current`. Local report `reports/phase2_h2/`. Tag `hypothesis=h2-season-def-regression`.
- H3: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h3`. Scores `h2_full`, `h3_split`, and `h3_replace` against logistic `h2_full`. Local report `reports/phase2_h3/`. Tag `hypothesis=h3-pass-rush-epa`.
- Ridge: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis ridge --reference-model logistic --reference-feature-set h2_full --output-dir reports/phase2_ridge`. Scores logistic `h2_full` and `logistic_l2` on `h2_full`, `h3_split`, and `h3_replace` against logistic `h2_full`. `logistic_l2` chooses C inside each training fold. The scored season is not used to pick C. Local report `reports/phase2_ridge/`. Tag `hypothesis=ridge-reference`.
- H4: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h4 --reference-model logistic --reference-feature-set h2_full --output-dir reports/phase2_h4`. Scores logistic `h2_full`, `h4_clean`, and `h4_clean_sr` against logistic `h2_full`, plus the home prior, Elo, and the market. Shrinkage, blend, and the garbage-time cutoffs are fixed. Local report `reports/phase2_h4/`. Tag `hypothesis=h4-clean-epa`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_h4`. Rebuild the Databricks marts first. Do not re-ingest. See `docs/experiments/phase2_h4_clean_epa.md`.
- H5: `python -m endzone.train.train --cv --phase 2 --hypothesis h5 --reference-model logistic --reference-feature-set h2_full --output-dir reports/phase2_h5`. Scores logistic `h2_full` and `h5_qb` against logistic `h2_full`, plus the home prior, Elo, and the market. QB shrinkage (100 prior dropbacks) and replacement EPA per dropback (0) are fixed. The QB-change subset is descriptive and is not an acceptance decision. Local report `reports/phase2_h5/`. Tag `hypothesis=h5-starting-qb`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_h5`. See `docs/experiments/phase2_h5_starting_qb.md`. The frozen snapshot is the original run. After the H5b depth-chart reload, this command reads the fixed starter too.
- H5b: `make train-cv` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-cv`). Same `h5_qb` features, same shrinkage, fixed starter only. Scores against logistic `h2_full`. Local report `reports/phase2_h5b/`. Tag `hypothesis=h5b-starter-coverage`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_h5b`. Rejected: `h5_qb` 0.6356, difference -0.0021, interval -0.0039 to -0.0002, short of -0.003. The threshold is not moved. See `docs/experiments/phase2_h5b_starter_coverage.md`.
- Recency: `make train-recency` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-recency`). `python scripts/train_recency.py` with no extra arguments. Four logistic variants against logistic `h2_full` on seasons 2016-2023. Local report `reports/phase2_recency/`. Tag `hypothesis=recency-streak`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_recency`. Not run. Do not use the walk-forward window, the 0.002 refresh margin, or the pretrained refresh to choose these variants. See `docs/experiments/recency_streak.md`.
- H6: `make train-h6` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-h6`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_h6.py` with no extra arguments. Logistic `h6_adj` and `h6_adj_elo` against logistic `h2_full` on seasons 2016-2023. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_h6/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=h6-opponent-adjusted`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_h6`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/h6_opponent_adjusted.md`.
- pkg_core: `make train-pkg-core` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-pkg-core`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_pkg_core.py` with no extra arguments. Logistic `pkg_core` against logistic `h2_full` on seasons 2016-2023. The same run also scores `h5_qb`, `recency_margin`, and `h6_adj_elo` for context under the same rule. `pkg_core` is the only preregistered candidate. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_pkg_core/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=pkg-core`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_pkg_core`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/pkg_core.md`.
- pkg_core_inj: `make train-pkg-core-inj` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-pkg-core-inj`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_pkg_core_inj.py` with no extra arguments. Logistic `pkg_core_inj` (C 1.0) and `pkg_core_inj_l2` (C fixed at 0.1, not tuned) against logistic `h2_full` on seasons 2016-2023. The same run also scores `pkg_core` for context. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_pkg_core_inj/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=pkg-core-inj`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_pkg_core_inj`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/pkg_core_inj.md`.
- Ensembles: `make train-ensembles` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-ensembles`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_ensembles.py` with no extra arguments. `gbm_pkg_core_inj` is `HistGradientBoostingClassifier` on the `pkg_core_inj_l2` columns with fixed `learning_rate` 0.05, `max_iter` 300, `max_leaf_nodes` 15, `min_samples_leaf` 50, `l2_regularization` 1.0, `random_state` 42, and no early stopping. Missing values stay missing. `ens_mean` is the unweighted per-fold mean of logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2` and that booster. No learned weights and no stacking. The reference is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. The same run also scores logistic `h2_full` for context. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration, per-season results, and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_ensembles/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=ensembles`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_ensembles`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/ensembles.md`.
- Ensembles r2: `make train-ensembles-r2` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-ensembles-r2`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_ensembles_r2.py` with no extra arguments. `ens_mean_elo` is the unweighted per-fold mean of logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2` and Elo. `stack_elo` is logistic regression on `logit(p_pkg_core_inj_l2)` and `logit(p_elo)`, with an intercept and C fixed at 1.0. Probabilities are clipped at 1e-6 before the logit. For outer season S the stacker is fit only on inner out-of-fold rows from 2010 through S-1. Members for inner season T train on seasons before T. The stacker does not see season S. The reference is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. The same run also scores logistic `h2_full`, Elo, and the market for context. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration, per-season results, stacker coefficients, and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. The market-information table names the model. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_ensembles_r2/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=ensembles_r2`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_ensembles_r2`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/ensembles_r2.md`.
- Prior shrink: `make train-prior-shrink` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-prior-shrink`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_prior_shrink.py` with no extra arguments. No dbt rebuild is required. `pkg_core_inj_l2_k39` is logistic regression on the `pkg_core_inj_l2` columns with the same names and order. Regressed season and within-season recent EPA uses blend k 3 on offense and k 9 on defense. Shrink stays 1/3. C is fixed at 0.1. `pkg_core_inj_l2_k39_decay` uses those columns and weights training rows by `0.5 ** ((last_train_season - season) / 5)`, computed on each fold's training seasons. Scoring is unweighted. Each candidate is judged alone against logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. The same run also scores logistic `h2_full`, Elo, `elo_mov`, and the market. `elo_mov` is a context probability from the gap plus home advantage 65 on a 400 scale. Its decision is `baseline`. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration, per-season results, and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_prior_shrink/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=prior_shrink`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_prior_shrink`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/prior_shrink.md`.
- QB Elo: `make train-qbelo538` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-qbelo538`). `PYTHONUTF8=1 MLFLOW_TRACKING_URI=databricks MLFLOW_REGISTRY_URI=databricks-uc uv run python scripts/train_qbelo538.py` with no extra arguments. Rebuild `fct_qb_box_scores` first. `pkg_core_inj_l2_qbelo538` is logistic regression on the `pkg_core_inj_l2` columns with `elo_mov_diff` replaced by `qbelo538_diff` and C fixed at 0.1. The starter is the depth-chart QB1 with the H5 fallback. A starter with no earlier game has adjustment 0. The VALUE weights, the 0.9 and 0.1 update, the 0.95 and 0.05 team update, and the 3.3 factor are the FiveThirtyEight values and are not tuned. `elo_mov` and `qbelo538` are context probabilities from the gap plus home advantage 65 on a 400 scale. Their decision is `baseline`. The reference is logistic `pkg_core_inj_l2`. The same run also scores logistic `h2_full`, Elo, and the market. The market row is `benchmark`, never `accepted`. Calibration, per-season results, QB coverage, and the market-information regression are in the report and are not gates. No blend is published. Local report `reports/phase2_qbelo538/comparison.md`. Tag `hypothesis=qbelo538`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/phase2_qbelo538`. Not run. See `docs/experiments/qbelo538.md`.
- EPA filter: `make check-epa-filter` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 check-epa-filter`). Writes `reports/epa_filter_check.md`. It does not change dbt models.
- Sprint 2: `make train-s2` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 train-s2`). `python -m endzone.modeling.points`. Scores ridge margin and ridge total against the Elo spread and the league-mean total. Local report `reports/sprint2/cv_report.json`. Tag `hypothesis=s2-margin-total`. Experiment `nfl_pregame/sprint2_score`. Registers `endzone-margin` and `endzone-total` only when that target passes. `make score` uses the same rule and writes null point estimates until both pass. See ADR-007.
- Registry: `make register-model` and `make promote-model VERSION=<n>` (Windows: `.\scripts\dev.ps1 register-model` and `promote-model`). This is not `make train-cv` and `make reproduce` does not call it. Experiment `nfl_pregame/registry` (Databricks: `/Shared/endzone-mlops/nfl_pregame/registry`). See ADR-009. `make register-model` stays through 2023. A `through_season` past 2023 without a walk-forward tag does not promote.
- Walk-forward: `make walk-forward SLATE_SEASON=2026 SLATE_WEEK=10` (Windows: set `SLATE_SEASON` and `SLATE_WEEK`, then `.\scripts\dev.ps1 walk-forward`). Same logistic `h2_full` is a refresh, not a challenger. The candidate refits on games before each week. v1 stays through 2023. Elo, the home rate, and the market are on the same games. Local report `reports/walk_forward/`. `make verify-walk-forward` is the gate: same recipe passes when pooled log loss is at most 0.002 above v1. A different model, feature set, or hyperparameter has to be strictly lower. The 0.003 rule is not moved and is not this gate. This is not a new phase. Weekly automation is future work. See `docs/experiments/walk_forward.md`. The warehouse pool is recorded there. `make register-recent` registers only a passing refresh and does not set the alias.

## Snapshots

`reports/` at the repo root is gitignored scratch. Do not commit it.

`docs/experiments/reports/` holds frozen snapshots. Add or replace one only when that hypothesis is decided. Do not hand-edit the numbers. Link each experiment note to its snapshot. The index is `docs/experiments/reports/README.md`.
